  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements :<br />Statement I : $\\mathrm{CrO}_3$ is a stronger oxidizing agent than $\\mathrm{MoO}_3$<br />Statement II : $\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{VI})$ is more stable than $\\mathrm{Mo}(\\mathrm{VI})$<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the<br />correct answer from the options given below",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wfoWt",
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YV5Vt",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1ov6D",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Wngy8",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Statement-I is true but statement II is false.<br />$\\mathrm{Cr}(\\mathrm{VI})$ is less stable than $\\mathrm{Mo}(\\mathrm{VI})$<br />Hence, $\\mathrm{CrO}_3$ easily reduce into $\\mathrm{Cr}^{+3}$ as compared to $\\mathrm{MoO}_3$ and show stronger oxidizing nature.",
    "image": null
